  "details": "I am making an avatar,\n\nThis is a bug that happened when I used my personal mirror.\n\nI have the same environment, but it doesn't show up on my own, \n\nBut when other people see me in their personal mirror, it looks like the picture on the left.\n\nWhen other people see me in their personal mirror, they can see the mesh behind the outlines\n\nThe bug is that the mesh behind the outline is displayed in a different place.\n\nThe shaders are liltoon only, and the part of the image that is displayed as a bug is opaque, and the culling mode is only applied to the front of the image.\n\n There is no abnormality in the normal viewpoint,\n\nWe have received a report that the bug occurs when using Personal Mirror Settings→Masking→Remote Player.\n\n The actual location of the bug was far from where I was.\n\nIt may be difficult to understand the DeepL translation from Japanese, but I will report it.",
